+## Session expiry
+
+`save_session` records an `issued_at` timestamp (seconds since the epoch) in each session. A
+session older than `SESSION_TTL` (3600 seconds) is rejected by `load_session` with
+`SessionExpiredError`; a session with a missing or future `issued_at` is rejected too.
+
+`purge_expired()` removes expired entries from the on-disk cache (`/tmp/sessioncache`) and is
+called at the start of every `load_session`.
+
+The resume blob is base64-encoded JSON, not pickle. `issued_at` inside a client-held blob is not
+signed, so a client could forge it; sign blobs before relying on the TTL against hostile clients.
